gm-method (static-file server symlink-escape guard 404s linked deps): a static handler that rejects symlinks whose realpath escapes the served mount (anti-traversal hardening) will silently 404 legitimate file:/workspace/pnpm-linked node_modules packages, since their real files live outside the mount by design. An ES-module import of such a package throws on the 404, aborting the importer's module graph -> the app's top-level init never runs -> a STATIC HTML placeholder (e.g. a click-to-play prompt) sits visible and looks like a stuck load, with window globals (scene/app/state-machine) all undefined. Diagnose via a browser witness capturing failed responses (status>=400) + whether window.* init globals exist, NOT by eyeballing the overlay. Fix: exempt symlinks whose LEXICAL path is under a node_modules segment from the realpath escape check (the lexical .. containment check already prevents attacker-chosen traversal in the request URL). Symlinked node_modules + server static handler is the recurring trap."}